Article 2 These Regulations shall apply to the safety supervision and administration of the following civil nuclear facilities:
(1) Nuclear power plants (nuclear power plants, nuclear heating plants, nuclear steam and heat supply plants, etc.);
(2) Reactors other than nuclear power plants (research reactors, experimental reactors, critical assemblies, etc.);
(3) Nuclear fuel production, processing, storage and reprocessing facilities;
(4) Radioactive waste treatment and disposal facilities;
(5) Other nuclear facilities requiring strict supervision and administration.

Article 4 The National Nuclear Safety Administration shall exercise unified supervision over the safety of nuclear facilities nationwide and independently exercise the authority of nuclear safety supervision, and its main functions are:
(1) Organizing the drafting and formulation of regulations on nuclear facility safety and reviewing technical standards on nuclear safety;
(2) Organizing the review and assessment of the safety performance of nuclear facilities and the capability of nuclear facility operating entities to ensure safety, and being responsible for issuing or revoking nuclear facility safety permits;
(3) Being responsible for implementing nuclear safety supervision;
(4) Being responsible for the investigation and handling of nuclear safety accidents;
(5) Coordinating with relevant departments to guide and supervise the formulation and implementation of emergency plans for nuclear facilities;
(6) Organizing relevant departments to carry out scientific research, publicity and education, and international business contacts on the safety and management of nuclear facilities;
(7) Mediating and adjudicating nuclear safety disputes jointly with relevant departments.

Article 6 The competent department of nuclear facilities shall be responsible for the safety management of the nuclear facilities under it, and shall accept the nuclear safety supervision of the National Nuclear Safety Administration. Its main functions are:
(1) Being responsible for the safety management of the nuclear facilities under its purview, ensuring necessary support to the operating entities of such nuclear facilities, and supervising and inspecting them;
(2) Participating in the drafting and formulation of relevant nuclear safety regulations, organizing the formulation of relevant technical standards on nuclear safety, and reporting them to the National Nuclear Safety Administration for record;
(3) Organizing the formulation and implementation of on-site emergency plans for the nuclear facilities under its purview, and participating in the formulation and implementation of off-site emergency plans;
(4) Being responsible for the technical training and assessment of all types of personnel at the nuclear facilities under its purview;
(5) Organizing scientific research work on nuclear safety in the development of nuclear energy.

Article 7 The nuclear facility operating entity shall be directly responsible for the safety of the nuclear facility it operates. Its main functions are:
(1) Complying with relevant national laws, administrative regulations and technical standards to ensure the safety of the nuclear facility;
(2) Accepting the nuclear safety supervision of the National Nuclear Safety Administration, reporting safety conditions in a timely and truthful manner, and providing relevant materials;
(3) Assuming overall responsibility for the safety of the nuclear facility it operates, the safety of nuclear materials, and the safety of workers, the public and the environment.

Article 8 The State shall implement a nuclear facility safety licensing system, and the National Nuclear Safety Administration shall be responsible for formulating and approving the issuance of nuclear facility safety permits, which include:
(1) Nuclear facility construction permits;
(2) Nuclear facility operation permits;
(3) Nuclear facility operator licenses;
(4) Other documents requiring approval.

Article 12 A "Nuclear Facility Construction Permit" or "Nuclear Facility Operation Permit" may be issued only if the following conditions are met:
(1) The applied project has been approved by the competent department and the State planning department or the planning department of the province, autonomous region or municipality directly under the Central Government in accordance with relevant regulations;
(2) The selected site has been approved by the State Council or the department of urban and rural construction and environmental protection, the planning department of the province, autonomous region or municipality directly under the Central Government, and the National Nuclear Safety Administration;
(3) The nuclear facility applied for conforms to the provisions of relevant national laws and nuclear safety regulations;
(4) The applicant has the capability to safely operate the applied nuclear facility and undertakes to assume full safety responsibility.

Article 14 An "Operator License" may be issued only if the following conditions are met:
(1) Good health, with no occupational contraindications;
(2) Having at least a secondary specialized school education or equivalent, and for nuclear power plant operators, having at least a college or higher education or equivalent;
(3) Having received operational training and having passed the assessment.
A "Senior Operator License" may be issued only if the following conditions are met:
(1) Good health, with no occupational contraindications;
(2) Having at least a college or higher education or equivalent;
(3) Having received operational training and having passed the assessment;
(4) Having served as an operator for more than two years with outstanding performance.

Article 16 The National Nuclear Safety Administration and its representative offices may station supervision teams (supervisors) at the sites of nuclear facility manufacturing, construction and operation to perform the following nuclear safety supervision tasks:
(1) Examining whether the submitted safety information conforms to reality;
(2) Supervising whether construction is carried out in accordance with the approved design;
(3) Supervising whether management is carried out in accordance with the approved quality assurance program;
(4) Supervising whether the construction and operation of nuclear facilities comply with relevant nuclear safety regulations and the conditions specified in the "Nuclear Facility Construction Permit" and "Nuclear Facility Operation Permit";
(5) Assessing whether operating personnel have the capability for safe operation and implementation of emergency plans;
(6) Other tasks requiring supervision.
Nuclear safety supervisors shall be appointed by the National Nuclear Safety Administration and issued with a "Nuclear Safety Supervisor Certificate".

Article 21 Whoever violates the provisions of these Regulations and commits any of the following acts, the National Nuclear Safety Administration may, depending on the severity of the circumstances, impose a penalty of a warning, ordering rectification within a time limit, suspending work or operations for rectification, or revoking the nuclear safety permit:
(1) Engaging in the construction, operation, relocation, transfer or decommissioning of a nuclear facility without approval or in violation of regulations;
(2) Falsely reporting relevant materials or facts, or refusing supervision without justifiable reasons;
(3) Operating without a license or operating in violation of regulations;
(4) Refusing to implement compulsory orders.
